# Every change needs the owner's review. With a branch ruleset that requires
# review from Code Owners, this is what stops an unapproved merge — including
# from a fork.
#
# The security-critical paths are listed separately not because the rule differs
# today, but so that adding a second maintainer later cannot accidentally hand
# over tenant isolation or authentication along with everything else.

* @hackermike

# Tenant isolation, auth, and audit — a mistake here is a PHI disclosure.
/app/tenancy.py      @hackermike
/app/auth/           @hackermike
/app/security/       @hackermike
/app/audit.py        @hackermike
/app/phi.py          @hackermike
/migrations/         @hackermike

# Workflow definitions run with repository permissions.
/.github/            @hackermike
